  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Soutien &#xe0; la reprise de l&apos;Ukraine pour la transparence, la r&#xe9;silience et l&apos;autonomisation</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine recovery support for transparency, resilience and empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Ce projet vise &#xe0; soutenir les efforts du gouvernement ukrainien pour renforcer la planification et la mise en &#x153;uvre d&#xe9;centralis&#xe9;es de la reconstruction. Les activit&#xe9;s de ce projet comprennent : 1) former les autorit&#xe9;s nationales comp&#xe9;tentes en mati&#xe8;re d&#x2019;analyse comparative entre les sexes + (ACS+) afin de renforcer leur capacit&#xe9; &#xe0; mettre en &#x153;uvre des initiatives de reconstruction inclusives; 2) soutenir le minist&#xe8;re national de la reconstruction afin de renforcer sa capacit&#xe9; d&#x2019;analyse et de communication des donn&#xe9;es relatives &#xe0; la reconstruction; 3) former et soutenir les autorit&#xe9;s locales en mati&#xe8;re de planification strat&#xe9;gique, de gestion de projet et de communication des r&#xe9;sultats; 4) former et soutenir les organisations locales de la soci&#xe9;t&#xe9; civile afin de renforcer leur capacit&#xe9; &#xe0; repr&#xe9;senter les collectivit&#xe9;s vuln&#xe9;rables; 5) accorder des financements &#xe0; certains projets locaux de reconstruction.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the Government of Ukraine&#x2019;s efforts to strengthen decentralized recovery planning and implementation. Project activities include: (1) training in Gender-Based Analysis+ (GBA+) to relevant national authorities to strengthen their capacity to deliver inclusive recovery initiatives; (2) supporting the national Ministry for Restoration to strengthen its capacity to analyze and communicate recovery data; (3) training and supporting local authorities on strategic planning, project management and results reporting; (4) training and supporting local civil society organizations to strengthen their capacity to represent vulnerable communities; and (5) granting funding to selected local recovery projects.</narrative>
  </description>
